WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.275
Nonforfeiture options.

2
00:00:02.636 --> 00:00:07.988
Here's what happens to a policy's cash value when the owner stops paying premiums.

3
00:00:08.917 --> 00:00:13.049
Permanent insurance, like whole life, charges a level premium.

4
00:00:13.503 --> 00:00:16.745
In the early years, that premium is more than the cost of the coverage,

5
00:00:16.765 --> 00:00:18.738
and the extra builds cash value.

6
00:00:19.401 --> 00:00:22.980
In this example, a one-hundred-thousand-dollar policy has built twenty thousand

7
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.866
dollars of cash value after fifteen years.

8
00:00:26.668 --> 00:00:28.931
That value belongs to the policyowner,

9
00:00:29.292 --> 00:00:33.986
and Arizona's nonforfeiture law says it can't simply be forfeited when premiums

10
00:00:34.006 --> 00:00:35.398
stop.

11
00:00:36.324 --> 00:00:39.237
So when the premiums stop, the owner has three choices,

12
00:00:39.331 --> 00:00:41.582
called nonforfeiture options.

13
00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.446
Option one is cash surrender.

14
00:00:44.738 --> 00:00:48.208
The owner takes the cash value, here twenty thousand dollars,

15
00:00:48.302 --> 00:00:50.066
and the coverage ends completely.

16
00:00:50.519 --> 00:00:55.476
One tax point the exam likes: if the cash received is more than the premiums paid,

17
00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.553
that gain is taxable as ordinary income.

18
00:00:59.479 --> 00:01:02.183
Option two is reduced paid-up insurance.

19
00:01:02.358 --> 00:01:05.086
The cash value is used to buy a smaller policy,

20
00:01:05.145 --> 00:01:07.129
here about thirty-five thousand dollars.

21
00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:11.611
It's the same type of permanent insurance, and it's fully paid up,

22
00:01:11.786 --> 00:01:13.654
so no more premiums are ever due.

23
00:01:14.201 --> 00:01:16.719
And it lasts for the insured's whole life.

24
00:01:17.665 --> 00:01:20.056
Option three is extended term insurance.

25
00:01:20.509 --> 00:01:23.783
The owner keeps the full one-hundred-thousand-dollar face amount,

26
00:01:23.958 --> 00:01:27.742
but the cash value buys term coverage instead of permanent coverage.

27
00:01:28.195 --> 00:01:32.912
It lasts only as long as that money can buy, in this example about eighteen years,

28
00:01:32.932 --> 00:01:34.336
and then it expires.

29
00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:36.484
If the owner doesn't pick an option,

30
00:01:36.543 --> 00:01:40.617
extended term is usually the one that applies automatically.

31
00:01:41.546 --> 00:01:43.461
Here's an easy way to keep them straight.

32
00:01:43.914 --> 00:01:48.128
Cash surrender: take the cash, and the coverage is gone.

33
00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:53.039
Reduced paid-up: less coverage, but for life.

34
00:01:53.493 --> 00:01:57.033
Extended term: the same amount of coverage, for a limited time.

35
00:01:57.487 --> 00:02:01.305
And for the exam, remember: when the owner doesn't choose,

36
00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:04.080
the insurer usually applies extended term.
